# The global default theme, used by mux-style when a session sets no @mux-theme
# and its context supplies no theme of its own. The colour is cosmetic; a
# context's banner/title marker shows regardless of the theme. Per-context theme
# overrides live in the context hook ($MUX_DIR/context), not here.
default         purple

# derive: how a session with no `theme` of its own gets one.
#   hash  pick deterministically from the session NAME, so every project wears
#         a stable colour with nothing configured -- and two projects only
#         share one by coincidence, which `mux theme` fixes in one keystroke.
#   off   every such session falls back to `default` above.
# A profile's own `theme`, and a context's theme, both still win over this.
#
# NOTE: the choice is an index into the sorted theme set, so ADDING or REMOVING
# a theme reshuffles the colours of every session that has not pinned one.
# Cosmetic, and pinning one you like makes it stick.
derive          hash
